=begin
  demonmana.lic
  A minor demon can hold a little mana (gswiki Minor_Summoning_(725), Minor Demon
  Abilities): base + Demonology bonus / 10 -- an igaesha 12 + 15 = ~28 at a
  bonus of 152, a verlok 0 + (15 - 3) = ~12, an aishan none. Sending costs a bit
  more than arrives and getting it back loses a bit more (10.19: 30 spent -> 28
  stored -> 26 back), but the demon can be filled while you rest and emptied in
  the middle of a hunt. Asking for more than it holds is harmless ("does not have
  that much mana so it resolves to send 28").

    ;demonmana send    send it all the mana it can hold   (mdemon_refresh does this while you rest)
    ;demonmana get     ask it for all of it back          (attack-ultima / sac4mana, once a hunt, when low)

  Which demon, and under what noun, comes from a silent TELL MDEMON RETURN (it also calls
  the demon back to the room first if it had wandered off).

  The first send to a demon shows how much it accepts (its capacity). If that's under
  MIN_STORE (20) the demon is skipped from then on -- no more sends, and no get --
  until it's replaced by a new one, which is measured afresh.

  Silver can be held too; not done here.
=end

SEND_OK  = /(\d+) points were succes+fully transferred to your .+? while only draining (\d+) mana points/i
GOT_MANA = /You gain (\d+) mana points/i
GONE     = /could not find|what were you referring/i

# A demon that holds less than this isn't worth the ~30 mana a send costs (10.19: a
# silver verlok'asha held 15 and gave back 7; an igaesha held 28 and gave back 26).
MIN_STORE = 20

# TELL MDEMON RETURN answers with the demon's id, noun and current name -- whatever illusion
# it wears (10.23: an imp as a "gnoll", "wizened gnoll" in the reply, "stooped and wizened
# gnoll" in the room) -- and calls it back if it had wandered off. SEND needs that noun:
# `send 50 gnoll` works, `send 50 mdemon` never does. Replies (all carry the link):
#   But your <a>X</a> is already here!  You're not playing games on it, are you?
#   Your <a>X</a> acknowledges your order and begins to travel to your location.
#   The magic in your location is interfering with your <a>X</a> returning to you.
RETURN_REPLY = /already here!|acknowledges your order|interfering with your|You have no minor demon at this time/i
DEMON_LINK   = %r{(?:[Bb]ut your|Your|your) <pushBold/><a exist="(\d+)" noun="([\w,'-]+)">([\w\-' ]+)</a><popBold/>}
ARRIVE_WAIT  = 60   # secs to wait for a called-back demon while resting; GET_WAIT in the middle of a hunt
GET_WAIT     = 10

def here?(id)
  (GameObj.npcs.to_a + GameObj.loot.to_a + GameObj.room_desc.to_a).any? { |o| o.id.to_s == id.to_s }
end

# => { id:, noun:, name:, here: } for your minor demon, or nil (said why). Asked silently.
def demon(wait = ARRIVE_WAIT)
  text = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("tell mdemon return", RETURN_REPLY).to_a.join("\n")
  unless text =~ DEMON_LINK
    echo(text =~ /no minor demon/i ? "you have no minor demon." : "no answer to TELL MDEMON RETURN.")
    return nil
  end
  d = { id: $1, noun: $2, name: $3, here: text.include?("already here!") }
  if text.include?("begins to travel")
    echo "your #{d[:name]} wasn't here -- waiting for it to arrive."
    wait.times { break if (d[:here] = here?(d[:id])); sleep 1 }
  end
  d
end

# What the first send to the current demon showed: { id:, points: } -- the points it
# accepted are its capacity. A new demon (new id) gets one send to find out.
def low_capacity?(d)
  c = $demonmana_cap
  !!(c && c[:id] == d[:id] && c[:points] < MIN_STORE)
end

def skip_note(d)
  c = $demonmana_cap
  echo "your #{d[:name]} holds only #{c[:points]} mana (under #{MIN_STORE}) -- not worth it, skipping." unless c[:said]
  c[:said] = true
end

def send_mana
  d = demon
  return unless d
  return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here -- not sending.") unless d[:here]
  return skip_note(d) if low_capacity?(d)
  waitrt?
  r = dothistimeout("send 50 #{d[:noun]}", 4, Regexp.union(SEND_OK, GONE, /cannot|can't|unable|already|too much/i)).to_s
  if r =~ SEND_OK
    $demonmana_cap = { id: d[:id], points: $1.to_i }
    echo "demon holds #{$1} mana now (#{$2} drained)."
  elsif r =~ GONE
    echo "couldn't find your #{d[:noun]} to send mana to."
  else
    echo "send said: #{r.strip[0, 120].empty? ? 'nothing' : r.strip[0, 120]}"
  end
end

def get_mana
  d = demon(GET_WAIT)
  return unless d
  return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here -- can't ask it for mana.") unless d[:here]
  return skip_note(d) if low_capacity?(d)
  waitrt?
  r = dothistimeout("tell mdemon send 50", 4, Regexp.union(GOT_MANA, GONE, /has no mana|any mana|nothing to send/i)).to_s
  if r =~ GOT_MANA
    echo "got #{$1} mana back from the demon."
  else
    echo "no mana from the demon (#{r.strip[0, 100].empty? ? 'no answer' : r.strip[0, 100]})."
  end
end

case script.vars[1].to_s.downcase
when 'send' then send_mana
when 'get'  then get_mana
else echo "usage: ;demonmana send   |   ;demonmana get"
end
